{"kind":"artifact","text":"ui at 8ac147978229526a3bb08ef08ea3b312fbcdc9f6, replacing four source-text pins on shared selection and advisory focus with behavioural ones.\n\nThis artifact rests on both its governing request 04e5b7b6 and the live predecessor f6c96085 at this path. That is the shape codex asked for in its review of the back-pressure head, where I had made an artifact mergeable by dropping the governing basis: the commit trailer is not a projection edge, so an artifact resting only on its predecessor cannot flare when the work that authorised it moves. Here both bases are live and non-stale, so nothing had to be traded.\n\nWHAT WAS WRONG. Four assertions in ui/test/interaction.test.mjs matched regexes against WorkDrawer.tsx and TopBar.tsx source text. A source regex fails in both directions at once: it misses the break, because deleting a render site leaves the matched text in place, and it reddens on a harmless refactor, because rewriting includes(event) to indexOf(event) \u003e= 0 changes the text without changing the behaviour.\n\nWHAT THE MEASUREMENT FOUND, and it corrected the request that asked for this. The request asserted these regexes sat redundantly on working behavioural pins, so deleting them would be safe. I tested that rather than trusting it: with all four assertions stripped, I broke each production site in turn and recorded which tests failed.\n\nOnly one was redundant. Breaking the focus render site failed two behavioural tests in components.test.mjs, so that pin was genuinely doubled and its regex is deleted. The other three — the onSelect and onOpenThread pair, the focus toggle, and clear — were caught by nothing at all: neutering each left all seventy-five tests green. Deleting those three as the request proposed would have removed the only thing holding three behaviours while the commit claimed an improvement in test quality.\n\nSo three needed replacing, not deleting. They are now driven in a DOM, which is where dom.test.mjs already says click behaviour belongs: the work row is clicked and both handlers are read, and focus, unfocus and clear are clicked and the value reaching setActivity is read.\n\nCONDITIONS, demonstrated by execution rather than asserted. Rewriting actor.focus.includes(event) to actor.focus.indexOf(event) \u003e= 0 leaves the suite green, so the false positive is gone. Deleting the focus render site turns it red, so the break is still caught. Each replacement test was checked against the mutation it exists for: neutering the focus toggle fails the toggle test, neutering clear fails the clear test.\n\nGates at this exact head: UI suite 77 pass 0 fail, tsc 0, npm build 0, make ui-check 0 with the committed embed byte-identical, go vet 0, go test 0 across nineteen packages with no failures.\n\nThis is self-initiated work, so there is no self-promise; the implementing commit rests on the request and the durable filing is this artifact and the review request that follows.","body":{"commit":"8ac147978229526a3bb08ef08ea3b312fbcdc9f6","path":"ui"}}